│ patch_description        │ I’m using a multiscale, parity-split quantum CNN-style block instead of independent       │
│                          │ per-qubit rotations plus a nearest-neighbor CZ chain.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The idea is to:                                                                           │
│                          │ - regularize strongly by sharing parameters across symmetry classes of qubits,            │
│                          │ - mix information locally with nearest-neighbor CNOTs,                                    │
│                          │ - inject long-range feature interactions directly with shared CRZ couplings,              │
│                          │ - and finish with a mirrored CZ pattern that couples opposite ends of the register.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This creates a hierarchical butterfly-like entangling structure that is better matched to │
│                          │ the fixed ZZ feature map: local correlations are captured first, then long-range phase    │
│                          │ information is propagated across the full 8-qubit register with far fewer effective       │
│                          │ degrees of freedom. That should improve generalization, reduce overfitting, and train     │
│                          │ efficiently under the fixed Adam loop.                                                    │
