│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ circular_cnot_efficient_ansatz                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This update optimizes the ansatz for better parameter efficiency and expressivity.        │
│                          │ 1.  **Replaced Linear CZ Chain with Circular CNOT Chain**: The previous design used a     │
│                          │ linear nearest-neighbor `CZ` chain (7 gates). A circular `CNOT` chain (8 gates, including │
│                          │ the [7, 0] wrap-around) provides stronger entanglement and better information flow across │
│                          │ all qubits, which is crucial for high-dimensional feature classification.                 │
│                          │ 2.  **Reduced Parameter Count**: The current ansatz (24 params/block) used two separate   │
│                          │ `RZ` layers. By condensing the rotations into a more standard `RY-CNOT-RZ` structure (16  │
│                          │ params/block), we reduce the total circuit parameters from 144 to 96 (a ~33% reduction).  │
│                          │ This significantly boosts the `parameter_efficiency` metric while maintaining enough      │
│                          │ capacity (6 total applications of the block) to keep accuracy high.                       │
│                          │ 3.  **Optimization Path**: The circular CNOT connectivity helps the model converge in     │
│                          │ fewer steps by providing more direct paths for gradient flow between all qubit pairs      │
│                          │ across the multiple re-uploading stages.                                                  │
