│ patch_name               │ add_controlled_entanglement_with_individual_params                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent accuracy (0.99) but has slow convergence (390      │
│                          │ steps) due to aggressive parameter sharing. Prior program 2 achieved better convergence   │
│                          │ (180 steps) with individual RY and RZ gates.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight: the trade-off between parameter count and convergence speed is           │
│                          │ non-linear. The current design (86 params, 390 steps) has worse overall efficiency than   │
│                          │ prior 2 (146 params, 180 steps).                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed improvement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Restore individual RY and RZ pre gates for per-qubit expressiveness (16 params per     │
│                          │ block)                                                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Add strategically placed CRZ (controlled-RZ) parametrized gates on non-adjacent qubits │
│                          │ (0-2, 2-4, 4-6) to enhance mid-range entanglement without creating a fully-connected      │
│                          │ entangling layer                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Keep individual RZ post gates (8 params per block)                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Provides 27 unique params per block (vs 24 in prior 2's successful configuration)       │
│                          │ - Enables finer per-qubit control while maintaining controlled two-qubit interactions     │
│                          │ - Should reduce convergence steps significantly (back toward ~200-250) while preserving   │
│                          │ high accuracy                                                                             │
│                          │ - Total params ≈ 164 (reasonable middle ground between 86 and 146)                        │
