│ patch_name               │ strongly_entangling_cnot_v1                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (Score 1.24, 86 params) uses a linear CZ chain and limited rotation    │
│                          │ variety. While accurate, it shows slower convergence (390 steps) and higher training loss │
│                          │ (0.16) compared to more expressive designs.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve the `combined_score`, I propose a "Strongly Entangling" block structure that   │
│                          │ utilizes all three rotation axes (RX, RY, RZ) and a two-stage CNOT entanglement pattern.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Gate Diversity**: Adding RX rotations alongside RY and RZ ensures the ansatz can     │
│                          │ reach any point on the Bloch sphere more efficiently, facilitating faster convergence.    │
│                          │ 2. **Entanglement**: Replacing the linear CZ chain with a two-layer circular CNOT pattern │
│                          │ (even pairs then odd pairs) improves the propagation of quantum correlations across the   │
│                          │ 8-qubit register.                                                                         │
│                          │ 3. **Parameter Allocation**: I've assigned 8 independent parameters each to RX and RY     │
│                          │ layers to maximize expressivity, while using a shared 4-parameter scheme for the RZ       │
│                          │ layer. This results in 20 parameters per block (122 total), providing a balance between   │
│                          │ the capacity of Seed 2 (146 params) and the efficiency of the current model.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This configuration aims to lower the training loss and accelerate convergence while       │
│                          │ maintaining high generalization.                                                          │
