                         Patch Metadata - Gen 11/20 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_params_across_uploads                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Following the recommendation to improve parameter efficiency while maintaining model      │
│                          │ expressiveness, this implementation shares the same parameter block across all uploads    │
│                          │ within each repeat index. Instead of allocating `N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK * N_UPLOADS *         │
│                          │ N_REPEATS` parameters, we now use only `N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK * N_REPEATS` by reindexing     │
│                          │ blocks with modulo arithmetic in `apply_ansatz_block`.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces total circuit parameters from 144 to 48 (with a 24-parameter block),         │
│                          │ yielding only 50 total trainable parameters. The architecture maintains the triple-upload │
│                          │ structure for data re-uploading while eliminating redundant parameter copies across       │
│                          │ uploads. Each of the 2 repeats within an upload has independent parameters, but these     │
│                          │ parameters are reused identically across all 3 uploads, preserving expressiveness while   │
│                          │ dramatically reducing overfitting risk and improving generalization.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key changes:                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. Apply `block_index % N_REPEATS` modulo operation in `apply_ansatz_block` to map all 6  │
│                          │ blocks (3 uploads × 2 repeats) to only 2 unique parameter positions                       │
│                          │ 2. Adjust `N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS` calculation to use only `N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK * N_REPEATS`     │
│                          │ instead of `N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK * N_UPLOADS * N_REPEATS`                                   │
│                          │ 3. Use the high-quality ansatz from the second program (full independent RZ parameters)   │
│                          │ as the base architecture                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency metric increases (fewer params achieving similar accuracy)         │
│                          │ - Better generalization (reduced parameter count lowers overfitting)                      │
│                          │ - Faster convergence through simpler optimization landscape                               │
│                          │ - Lower test loss through improved regularization                                         │
