│ patch_description        │ This edit compresses the block to four trainable angles per repeated ansatz block while   │
│                          │ keeping strong data-driven mixing.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency improves materially: 4 shared circuit parameters per block instead │
│                          │ of 5, dropping total trainable parameters from 32 to 26.                                  │
│                          │ - The entangler pattern becomes a small-world graph: local CZ pairs preserve the useful   │
│                          │ inductive bias from the binary feature map, while two long-range bridges connect the two  │
│                          │ halves of the register and help information flow across the whole 8-qubit system.         │
│                          │ - Using shared parity-based RY and half-register RZ layers reduces overfitting pressure   │
│                          │ and usually converges faster under Adam on re-uploading classifiers.                      │
│                          │ - Gate count also falls slightly, which should help the combined score without            │
│                          │ sacrificing the proven re-uploading structure.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The change stays fully within the allowed ANSATZ_SPEC schema and preserves the fixed      │
│                          │ training loop and readout.                                                                │
