│                          │ the requested sparse long-range controlled-phase motif.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Share parameters across even/odd qubits for the initial RY layer to cut redundant       │
│                          │ degrees of freedom.                                                                       │
│                          │ - Keep a shallow CZ backbone to preserve fast entanglement spread.                        │
│                          │ - Use a compact 3-way shared RZ pattern for phase refinement instead of per-qubit phase   │
│                          │ freedom.                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Add a single shared CRZ parameter on three cross-register pairs to capture nonlocal     │
│                          │ correlations efficiently.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should reduce train-test gap and validation loss, improve parameter efficiency, and  │
