│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_ring_mixer                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the current high-parameter block with a much more parameter-efficient, │
│                          │ symmetry-aware ansatz. The fixed data uploads already inject rich feature-dependent       │
│                          │ phases, so the candidate block should focus on lightweight non-commuting mixing rather    │
│                          │ than many independent single-qubit angles.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new block:                                                                            │
│                          │ - shares parameters across even/odd qubits to cut redundancy and regularize,              │
│                          │ - keeps a full CZ ring for cheap global entanglement,                                     │
│                          │ - adds a small number of long-range CRY couplings to mix distant registers,               │
│                          │ - ends with shared RZ refinement to recover phase flexibility.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should reduce the number of trainable circuit parameters substantially, lower depth  │
│                          │ and gate count, and improve convergence speed while preserving enough expressivity for    │
│                          │ the repeated re-uploading layout.                                                         │
